# -- every Rust string literal under core/*/src that is JavaScript (tests/js_strings.rs).
#
# The kernel defines Web API in one table per interface, in Rust. A member defined in a JS string is
# outside the ESM graph, invisible to the install ledger, and wins or loses by evaluation order. So
# this file should be EMPTY, and every row in it is a debt with a reason a reader can check.
#
# It fails in BOTH directions. A JS string that is not listed here fails the test. A row whose string
# is no longer in the tree fails it too -- delete the string and the row goes in the SAME commit.
# `scripts/freeze.sh`'s `js_strings_kernel` ratchet counts these rows, so the count only ever falls.
# Membership is DERIVED (never hand-curated); regenerating preserves the reason of every row whose
# `id` is unchanged, and writes REASON-REQUIRED for a new one, which fails until a human writes why.
#
# columns, tab-separated:  <path>  <id>  <excerpt>  <why this is allowed to exist>
# `id` is FNV-1a-64 of the literal's source text, so editing the string retires the row.
